From 278fe35d4056ee466bec10aa4684790e0c668403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:50:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Submit your team straight from your save, remember the
 dialog, curate the music

Guest save submission, after the design the community built for OrreLink's ancestor:
instead of a Showdown paste, "Use my save" reads the guest's own save locally,
extracts a small party-and-identity bundle -- the six party mons byte-for-byte,
trainer name, gender, TID and SID -- and sends that through the existing team
submission channel. The host rebuilds the guest's disposable socket-3 save from
the bundled template with the bundle's party AND its trainer identity, so the
mons' OT is the save's own trainer and obedience is intrinsically right; no
re-stamping happens anywhere on this path. Nicknames, ribbons and met history
survive because the real bytes ride the wire. The original save is only ever
read, the bundle is strictly validated host-side before anything else happens,
and the stash/restore/cleanup lifecycle is exactly the one every submitted team
already gets. The dialog says plainly that sending a party reveals its details
to the host's machine.

The submit dialog also finally remembers itself: team text, trainer name,
model pick and the use-my-save choice persist across sessions and prefill on
open, stored on successful submission.

And one music entry leaves the catalog: "Shadow Event" (id 7) is a sequenced
archive container, not a streamable track -- the original research excluded
that class and this one slipped through; the field test caught it as silence.

Version 1.3.1.
